;; wai's Go run corpus's classes (bin/wai go; doc/wasm/WAI.md §8; doc/wasm/WASM-SURVEY.md §10.2, WAS11 (a), WA5): every row of
;; test/wasm/go-results.edn that does not pass is in the first class that names it in :ids, else the first whose :match finds its
;; REASON, in goi's format. Read with the Clojure reader. The skips first (no judgment of wai: gc's own run does not pass, Go's test
;; driver would not run the program for wasip1/wasm, an action goi skips too), then what wasip1 has not (processes, mmap), then wai's.
[
 {:id :go-gc-skip
  :title "gc's own run does not pass the test here"
  :kind :na
  :why "the reference is gc's linux/amd64 run of the original, as goi's check's (RPS12): when gc's own run fails the test (a status not 0, output other than the golden .out) there is nothing to judge wai against, and goi skips the program too"
  :decided "WAS11 (a), the user 2026-11-13; goi's rule (report 002, finding 5)"
  :match [#"^gc's own run does not pass here"]}
 {:id :go-constraint
  :title "Go's test driver does not run the program for wasip1/wasm"
  :kind :na
  :why "cmd/internal/testdir's shouldTest evaluates the program's build constraints for GOOS and GOARCH; a program it would not run on wasip1/wasm (//go:build !wasm, amd64, linux, unix ...) is not a test of the port, as on every other port Go's own runner skips it"
  :decided "WAS11 (a), the user 2026-11-13 (the survey's §10.2: the programs Go's runner skips on wasm classed)"
  :match [#"^the test driver's build constraint excludes wasip1/wasm" #"^build constraints exclude wasip1/wasm"]}
 {:id :go-action
  :title "an action goi's check skips too"
  :kind :na
  :why "an action that sets -goexperiment or -godebug builds another toolchain configuration; goi's check skips it and wai's corpus keeps goi's rule"
  :decided "goi's check (doc/go/GOI-SPEC.md §11.1)"
  :match [#"^the action sets "]}
 {:id :go-speed
  :title "slower on wai than three times the action's limit"
  :kind :budget
  :why "wai interprets the Go program's whole wasm module (its runtime's start, its collector) one instruction at a time; a program that runs for seconds under gc runs past three times its action's limit (WAI_GO_SLOW) here: a matter of the budget, not of a result (w2g's AOT level, WA7, is the speed's answer)"
  :decided "WA5 (a proposal: WAS35)"
  :match [#"^timeout: "]}
]
